    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_2408da1ddb61d40ed129edf183aa40273905b3ba520c511a2011abf252b8d3d9",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The finite negative-integer formula obtained by truncating the continued series and resolving its exceptional term has two linked consequences: after q-to-1 rescaling, an alternating binomial operator annihilates intermediate degrees and isolates the classical Bernoulli coefficient; under the shifted definition B_m(q)=-m zeta_q(1-m), the same negative-value structure becomes a q-Bernoulli closed form, coefficient recursion, and generating-function dilation equation.",
