    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_468be0be8e0ace5097257e3c03fa82686a2af5d123c807e7af57da9a0ff9cf2c",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "At integer s=k, reindexing the q-zeta expansion produces a scaled Lambert series whose top polynomial degree survives the q-to-1 limit and yields zeta(k). For even k>=4, divisor-sum reorganization identifies that same Lambert series as the nonconstant Fourier part of an Eisenstein series, so modular inversion turns its q-boundary asymptotic into the Eisenstein constant term, equivalently expressed through zeta(k) and the Bernoulli number B_k.",
